==You are a product communication expert. Generate role-specific Slack messages for each relevant team from this product update.

Title: {{ $('Webhook').item.json.body.title }}
What was built: {{ $('Webhook').item.json.body.what_was_built }}
What users can now do: {{ $('Webhook').item.json.body.what_users_can_do }}
What changes for existing users: {{ $('Webhook').item.json.body.what_changes }}
Primary audience: {{ $('Webhook').item.json.body.audience }}
Submitted by: {{ $('Webhook').item.json.body.submitted_by }}

Generate a tailored Slack message for EACH of the following teams if they are in the Primary audience. If a team is not in the audience, set their message to null.

Message style per team:
- Sales: focus on customer value, competitive advantage, and what to pitch. Use confident, energetic language.
- Customer Success: focus on how to help customers adapt, what questions to expect, what changed. Use empathetic, practical language.
- Support: focus on what broke or changed, what tickets to expect, how to respond. Use clear, direct, actionable language.
- Engineering: focus on technical details, what was shipped, dependencies. Use precise, technical language.
- Marketing: focus on positioning, messaging opportunities, what to highlight externally. Use creative, brand-aware language.
- All Teams: a general company-wide message everyone can understand. Use simple, friendly language.

Return ONLY this JSON, nothing else, no backticks, no explanation:
{
  "sales_message": "Slack message for Sales under 100 words with emojis, or null",
  "cs_message": "Slack message for Customer Success under 100 words with emojis, or null",
  "support_message": "Slack message for Support under 100 words with emojis, or null",
  "engineering_message": "Slack message for Engineering under 100 words with emojis, or null",
  "marketing_message": "Slack message for Marketing under 100 words with emojis, or null",
  "general_message": "Slack message for All Teams under 100 words with emojis, or null",
  "cartoon_script": "Panel 1: [scene] - [dialogue]. Panel 2: [scene] - [dialogue]. Panel 3: [scene] - [dialogue]. Panel 4: [scene] - [dialogue]."
}

parameters.jsCode:
const items = $input.all();
const raw = items[0].json.content[0].text;
const parsed = JSON.parse(raw);
const audience = $('Webhook').item.json.body.audience;

let audienceArray = [];
if (typeof audience === 'string') {
  audienceArray = audience.split(',').map(a => a.trim());
} else if (Array.isArray(audience)) {
  audienceArray = audience;
} else {
  audienceArray = ["All Teams"];
}

const channelMap = {
  "Sales": { id: "C0B8UFBGWTG", message: parsed.sales_message },
  "Customer Success": { id: "C0B8YCGNVG9", message: parsed.cs_message },
  "Support": { id: "C0B90620W3W", message: parsed.support_message },
  "Engineering": { id: "C0B90631P8C", message: parsed.engineering_message },
  "Marketing": { id: "C0B9QRUL8G0", message: parsed.marketing_message },
  "All Teams": { id: "C0B8T60SQNR", message: parsed.general_message }
};

const channels = audienceArray
  .map(a => channelMap[a])
  .filter(c => c && c.message && c.message !== null);

return [{
  json: {
    channels: channels,
    cartoon_script: parsed.cartoon_script
  }
}];

const channels = $('Code in JavaScript').item.json.channels;
const binaryData = $input.item.binary.data;

return channels.map(channel => ({
  json: {
    channelId: channel.id,
    slack_message: channel.message
  },
  binary: {
    data: binaryData
  }
}));

